{"id": "EUVD-2026-55533", "enisaUuid": "69448d37-82ff-3291-a7b5-bb1d9a6d5a51", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nfscrypt: Add missing superblock check in find_or_insert_direct_key()\n\nThe legacy 'fscrypt_direct_keys' table caches master keys that are used\nby v1 encryption policies that have FSCRYPT_POLICY_FLAG_DIRECT_KEY.\nIt's just a global table for all filesystems (since the keys can be\nprovided by the legacy process-subscribed keyrings mechanism, which\nmakes it difficult to reuse super_block::s_master_keys).\n\nThe entries in it ('struct fscrypt_direct_key') do contain a super_block\npointer, though, for passing to fscrypt_destroy_inline_crypt_key() when\nthe last inode that references the key is evicted.\n\nHowever, when finding the fscrypt_direct_key for an inode, we weren't\nactually comparing the super_block pointer.  As a result, inodes with\ndifferent super_blocks could point to the same fscrypt_direct_key.  That\ncould extend the lifetime of a fscrypt_direct_key beyond the\nsuper_block it points to, causing a use-after-free later.\n\nFix this by creating distinct fscrypt_direct_key structs for distinct\nsuper_block structs.\n\nNote that this problem doesn't exist in the v2 policy equivalent\n(\"per-mode keys\"), since the data structures there are per super_block.", "datePublished": "2026-08-10T11:59:13", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-19T20:58:54", "baseScore": 7.8, "baseScoreVersion": "3.1", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:3.1/AV:L/AC:L/PR:L/UI:N/S:U/C:H/I:H/A:H", "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/965b5bc8cf5031225e057979ce660fec2bd5fbfc", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/330249609b70778094a7a36f5b6bcfa6362121d4", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/deff41898a5ae3a47db5fa1896a494aa95efda5d", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/95376fe9c145be35566991df99c53134943d992f", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/466f187b501a5ac8e1ea2ccf3ccd5c46108d8830", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/b5fa40226e71c17847b9ff2816c6ca4133d0d994"], "aliases": ["GHSA-r7wr-xw9j-768v", "CVE-2026-68148"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.09, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "10d27581-3785-358c-a462-f23baddd7010", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "22e9947a4b2ba255888541bd0111cf00b9b16586 <b5fa40226e71c17847b9ff2816c6ca4133d0d994"}, {"id": "340cbc2f-5b8c-370a-90e0-60bae4ff38bf", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.2"}, {"id": "481147a1-7026-36fe-9072-183f64fa75bc", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.18.42"}, {"id": "4fab735e-cd2a-302c-9684-44a1b288d3a2", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.1.6"}, {"id": "5c9a3958-1f8b-37fc-be91-94de5e1c8902", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.12.101"}, {"id": "5cc2cf1f-3633-36e6-a9df-e1ebfc913dd1", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "22e9947a4b2ba255888541bd0111cf00b9b16586 <466f187b501a5ac8e1ea2ccf3ccd5c46108d8830"}, {"id": "646d94dd-b177-3427-99fe-deab962f596d", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}, {"id": "6deb4788-6ed7-36ae-bcd7-3b0ad4c5db68", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.6.148"}, {"id": "813b60d1-1bab-3df1-bb28-464b084a09f1", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "6.1"}, {"id": "a4af5103-ff39-3cf2-8652-c115c5141117", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "22e9947a4b2ba255888541bd0111cf00b9b16586 <deff41898a5ae3a47db5fa1896a494aa95efda5d"}, {"id": "ae217b13-614b-3823-9c47-a92bbc110c47", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.1.183"}, {"id": "b0442891-80da-301b-8a96-9775fbbf7fb3", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "22e9947a4b2ba255888541bd0111cf00b9b16586 <330249609b70778094a7a36f5b6bcfa6362121d4"}, {"id": "cf83d1ce-e852-3f58-9cda-4f3c64073725", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "22e9947a4b2ba255888541bd0111cf00b9b16586 <965b5bc8cf5031225e057979ce660fec2bd5fbfc"}, {"id": "d1295d29-9128-35e5-bb59-ec666eaf603b", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "22e9947a4b2ba255888541bd0111cf00b9b16586 <95376fe9c145be35566991df99c53134943d992f"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "a1440080-a303-37b6-bb35-f6fc7307ce89", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}], "isExploited": false}